    <td>
<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Ultima Online 2 - UO2 Vault Chat with Ubiq and Windfeather for 6/28/2000</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>&lt;Quad_Energy[PT]&gt;</b> heh yah i want a bridge of fish
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Beast invented Bridge of Fish!
<br><b>&lt;Darkmane&gt;</b> Bridge of fish must stink.. literally :P
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Bridge of Fish was a joke when Ubiq said, 'Make fishing more useful!'
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Bridge of Fish won't make ship.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Unless you all petition for it.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Maybe a petition on the message boards could save it.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Beast would be very pleased if an upswelling of support from the fans restored it to the ship list.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Doozer&gt;</b> Wouldn't it make a kind of paradox if craftsmen had to gain the majority of their ankhs by fighting?  Then they'd have to spend 
  their time on fighting skills isntead of craft skills.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> We're workin' on that one, Doozer :)
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> It is a paradox.. and one that I don't understand completely.. as to fight, they will need to use skill points.
<br><b>&lt;Doozer&gt;</b> Right, Kyreg.  It's weird.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Doozer, that can't happen.  The cost of gaining skill points rise, and if you spend your ankhs on crafting things, your fighting ability doesn't rise with it.  
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Advancing your crafting by fighting things would be very inefficient.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Smity&gt;</b> Does anyone know how many characters we will get?
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Smity: Undecided, we want to reduce multi-character abuse, but one per shard may not be doable.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Dark_Matter|UH&gt;</b> Hey, you guys won't restrict us from having names, right? EQ restricted me from having Dark, then they took away Matter...I'm never going to touch the thing again
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Other than unique names, we have not formalized our name policy.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> You won't have any Ass Mastas in Origin.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> but agree with Windy, no AssMastas.
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> Doozer, well the problem is obvious, I suspect they have it solved.
<br><b>&lt;Doozer&gt;</b> *shrug* I hope, but they haven't said a thing about it.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Doozer&gt;</b>  we have a few plans, but until we choose one, I don't want to lead you all astray.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Tyrant will most likely be the one that determines the name policy.  I think he will end up with something that is fair.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Yep.  One the whole, I prefer some name filtering.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;G56&gt;</b> Windfeather have you guys been playing EQ?? (please say you havent)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> G56: I play everything :)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> I do not, however, LIKE everything.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Azul&gt;</b> Hey ubiq, what about shipping origin with a copy of Roger Wilco?  So everyone has it?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Azul&gt; Roger Wilco is peer to peer, and while it rocks, I don't want to claim that we support it and the issues that will come with it.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Peer to peer programs make your IP available, which good hackers can use tot heir advantage,for example, to pingbomb you.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> BTW:  I was a Guide in EQ.. and the name filter thing works in an interesting way.  There is human involvement when you create a character believe it or not.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Kyreg: I heard that...if someone is on, they can reject?
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> We did that at Simutronics.
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> That is correct.. if the name is not in the database, the guide is asked, and the guide can reject.
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> Once rejected, it is added to the database.
<br><b>&lt;Kyreg&gt;</b> It is really pretty clever.. I have kept many ass mastas out of EQ :)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Kyreg: I bet it did, and I like that...I have seen the flip side of the coin, too, where you get one guide on staff who has read every fantasy book ever published, and he becomes a name Nazi.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;G56&gt;</b> I hope you dont have any of the restrictions that EQ has!
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Like what?
<br><b>&lt;G56&gt;</b> Like making the world so simplistic and SETUP... town ---&gt;</b> level 1-4 monsters ---->" 5-8 monsters----&gt;</b> etc etc
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> G56: We'll tend to keep easier stuff near towns, but we do not have 'zones'.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> But with the fact that we have tech stuff in our game, we should be able to be a bit more lenient about what 'fits.'
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Azul&gt;</b> Is that game set up so a high level person could travel with a low level person and still have fun?  Unlike EQ where a level 50 wouldn't w/ lev 1
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Azul&gt; we in fact are hoping to encourage it.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Doozer&gt;</b> I just have to say that you guys are thinking of everything, and I'm GLAD :P
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Doozer&gt; We're all vets of the industry.  We're pretty sure we won't make the same old mistakes.  The question is how many NEW ones we'll make.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Never underestimate experience.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;G56&gt;</b> Windfeather :   Will you only gain "exp" from killing things that are near your level?
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> G56: I believe we will have a wide range, actually.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> g56, unlike a class-based system, your level doesn't accurately reflect your ability - it's based on how smartly you spent your skill trees, and how well you use those abilities
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Ripley&gt;</b> *How will u get rid of kill taking, and people hunting in groups that aren't in the same party?*
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Ripley: PvP solves a lot, in the safe lands we'll probably have to have something vaguely similar to EQ.
