<br><b>&lt;Azul&gt;</b> Ubiq:  WIll there be a time played tally in there?  I always love to see how much of my life I have put into a game...
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Azul, I've added it to the idea list
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Ripley&gt;</b> Ubiq: How many of the ideas on the stratics boards that you have seen have actually been added into the game that weren't planned to be added until they were on the boards??? Can u give any examples??
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Oh heck, I changed a few things in Death mechanics because of input.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> People pointed out lots of little niggling problems.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Ripley&gt; I have a massive file on my desktop called 'ideas from fans.doc'.  I review it frequently as we reexamine systems.  A surprising amount makes it in.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Azul&gt;</b> Does origin take place after Ultima Online, or on its own timeline?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Azul&gt; answer to that is on the faq
<br>
<br><b>&lt;G56&gt;</b> UBIQ :   How basically will beta testers be chosen?           IE: players who have had active accounts for x ammount of time and subscribe to uo2 newsletter?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> g56&gt; I cannot comment on the beta at all.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Dark_Matter|UH&gt;</b> Do you guys get to play the beta?
<br><b>&lt;Dark_Matter|UH&gt;</b> Or just continue to program like nuts
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> We'll be in there every day testing stuff.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Whol&gt;</b> For the most part I supported UO's "nerfs" I was all for elimination of recall for instance, but EQ's nerfs, like disabling the manastone in the planes, was simply because players were performing better in the planes than expected
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Whol&gt; a large part of that is their class system.  -I am not against class systems- but with UO, if your class got nerfd, you could always switch professions.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Whol: Do you think there was a better solution for the manastone...?
<br><b>&lt;Whol&gt;</b> even with my manastone I died plenty in Hate
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> I can't really say, since I never made the planes.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Wasn't there an infinite mana combo with manastones? =)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Manastone is a mana regen item, infinite charges.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> That help? :)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> They made it so it did not work in new high-level areas.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;GooGone&gt;</b> From the sound of it I guess I made a wise choice by not ever playing EQ, eh? You guys sound like it's the worst thing int he world.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> GooGone&gt; it's not the worst thing in the world.  It is a very different experience from UO.  Both are great games, and both have flaws.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> EQ is a monster bash, but I certainly enjoyed my stay there.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Dark_Matter|UH&gt;</b> I should hope you guys get your pick on the names first...it would be pretty funny if you tried to log in and it said your name was taken...
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> I don't think that would be a problem, Dark_Matter :)
<br>
<br><b>&lt;GooGone&gt;</b> UO2 / Origin needs the profession Barber! so we can change hairstyles whenever we want! :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> GooGone&gt; no comment.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Dark_Matter|UH&gt;</b> Oh ya, will the spell effects be something like counterstrike flashes?
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> I haven't seen the particles (spells) yet.
</font>

</td></tr></table>

